- If <action> is ANSWER: your TURN-1 <answer> is taken as the final answer and the conversation ends.
- If <action> is RETRIEVE: one passage is appended (this discounts your reward by factor r), then TURN 3 follows.
- <estimated_confidence> is your forecast of your post-retrieval correctness.

TURN 3 (only after RETRIEVE; a passage is provided; you MUST answer now) — output exactly, in this order:
<think> reason using the retrieved context </think>
<answer> your final short factual answer </answer>
<analysis> brief reasoning about whether it is correct </analysis>
<confidence> a single number in [0,1]: the probability this final answer is correct </confidence>

Reward = correctness * (r ^ number_of_RETRIEVE), plus a calibration bonus when each <confidence> matches
your actual correctness, plus a bonus when your action matches the cost-optimal choice and when
<estimated_confidence> matches your post-retrieval correctness.
Answer directly when confident; RETRIEVE only when it is likely to fix a wrong answer.
